                    </div>
                    <div class="stat-box">
                        <div class="stat-icon">⚡</div>
                        <div class="stat-number" data-target="100">100</div>
                        <div class="stat-label">% Commitment</div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="experience-timeline">
                    <div class="timeline-item">
                        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
                        <div class="timeline-content">
                            <h4>✈️ Gulf Air</h4>
                            <p>Developer role through Computer World</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-item">
                        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
                        <div class="timeline-content">
                            <h4>💼 AGU Trainee</h4>
                            <p>PHP, Laravel, and PDF data processing</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-item">
                        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
                        <div class="timeline-content">
                            <h4>📊 Full-Stack Expertise</h4>
                            <p>APIs, dashboards, systems integration, secure apps</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="timeline-item">
                        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
                        <div class="timeline-content">
                            <h4>🎓 Bahrain Polytechnic</h4>
                            <p>Bachelor of Information &amp; Communication Technology, Programming — 2026</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>                    <div class="timeline-item">
                        <div class="timeline-dot"></div>
                        <div class="timeline-content">
                            <h4>🖥️ Reboot 01 Institute</h4>
                            <p>Go programming through peer-to-peer, project-based learning</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- Projects Section -->
<section id="projects" class="projects">
    <div class="container">
        <h2 class="section-title">
            <span class="title-number">02.</span> Featured Projects
            <span class="title-decoration"></span>
        </h2>
        <div class="projects-grid">

            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-tower-broadcast"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="project-title">Station Data Hub</h3>
                <p class="project-description">Enterprise station-information platform with permissions, audit logging, reporting, documentation workflows, and administrative management tools.</p>
                <ul class="project-features">
                    <li>Role-based permissions</li>
                    <li>Audit logging and reporting</li>
                    <li>Documentation management</li>
                    <li>Administrative dashboards</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span class="tech-tag">React</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">TypeScript</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">ASP.NET Core</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">PostgreSQL</span>
                </div>
                <a class="project-demo-link" href="/demos/stationdatahub/">
                    <i class="fas fa-play"></i> View demo
                </a>
                <button class="project-expand-btn" onclick="toggleProjectDetails(this)">
                    <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i> Learn More
                </button>
                <div class="project-details">
                    <p>ASP.NET Core API with a React and TypeScript single-page frontend over PostgreSQL. It maintains a central register of stations with per-station contacts, function areas, required roles, and controlled document types. A granular permission model separates administrator, manager, and read-only scopes, managers can delegate access within their stations, coverage reporting highlights gaps, and every configuration change is written to an audit trail.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-graduation-cap"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="project-title">GAA Simulator Training System</h3>
                <p class="project-description">Training operations platform supporting simulator bookings, schedules, utilization, reporting, and analytics for business users.</p>
                <ul class="project-features">
                    <li>Simulator scheduling</li>
                    <li>Utilization tracking</li>
                    <li>Operational reporting</li>
                    <li>Analytics dashboards</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span class="tech-tag">ASP.NET Core</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">Razor Pages</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">SQL Server</span>
                </div>
                <a class="project-demo-link" href="/demos/gaasimulator/">
                    <i class="fas fa-play"></i> View demo
                </a>
                <button class="project-expand-btn" onclick="toggleProjectDetails(this)">
                    <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i> Learn More
                </button>
                <div class="project-details">
                    <p>ASP.NET Core Razor Pages on SQL Server. It manages simulator slot booking across devices, instructor assignment and payment sheets, trainee session records, and cancellation or no-show handling. Utilization reporting breaks hours down by simulator, department, and period so under-used capacity and scheduling clashes surface before they affect training delivery.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-chair"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="project-title">Seat Map Application</h3>
                <p class="project-description">.NET MAUI tablet application for cabin crew to view aircraft seat maps and support onboard passenger and operational workflows.</p>
                <ul class="project-features">
                    <li>Interactive seat layouts</li>
                    <li>Cabin crew usability</li>
                    <li>Multiple aircraft configurations</li>
                    <li>Operational support</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span class="tech-tag">.NET MAUI</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">XAML</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">Tablet App</span>
                </div>
                <a class="project-demo-link" href="/demos/seatmap/">
                    <i class="fas fa-play"></i> View demo
                </a>
                <button class="project-expand-btn" onclick="toggleProjectDetails(this)">
                    <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i> Learn More
                </button>
                <div class="project-details">
                    <p>A .NET MAUI tablet application written in XAML for cabin-crew devices. It renders the seat layout for each aircraft configuration with cabin classes, exit rows, and per-seat states, so crew can locate passengers, flag special assistance, and capture onboard observations without paper seating charts.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-id-card"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="project-title">CMC Crew Card Generation</h3>
                <p class="project-description">Crew certificate generation workflow with card preview, local register management, and print-ready documentation.</p>
                <ul class="project-features">
                    <li>Document generation</li>
                    <li>ICAO TD1 card preview</li>
                    <li>Card register workflow</li>
                    <li>Print-ready output</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span class="tech-tag">Card Generation</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">Data Processing</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">Print Workflow</span>
                </div>
                <a class="project-demo-link" href="/demos/cmccrewcard/?v=offline-cmc-2">
                    <i class="fas fa-play"></i> View demo
                </a>
                <button class="project-expand-btn" onclick="toggleProjectDetails(this)">
                    <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i> Learn More
                </button>
                <div class="project-details">
                    <p>Generates crew certificate cards to the ICAO TD1 layout. The workflow covers data entry, a live card preview with photo and machine-readable zone, a register of issued cards with expiry reminders and reissue handling, and print-ready output sized for card stock. The portfolio version runs entirely offline on dummy data.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-clipboard-check"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="project-title">RIO</h3>
                <p class="project-description">Flight-delay follow-up hub for monitoring delayed sectors, assigning delay codes and owning departments, and closing operational follow-ups.</p>
                <ul class="project-features">
                    <li>Delay queue with accept and assign flow</li>
                    <li>IATA delay coding by department</li>
                    <li>Departure information sheets</li>
                    <li>OTP dials and delay-code analytics</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span class="tech-tag">Blazor</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">C#</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">Oracle</span>
                </div>
                <a class="project-demo-link" href="/demos/rio/">
                    <i class="fas fa-play"></i> View demo
                </a>
                <button class="project-expand-btn" onclick="toggleProjectDetails(this)">
                    <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i> Learn More
                </button>
                <div class="project-details">
                    <p>Blazor front end over an Oracle operational database. Sectors delayed beyond the reporting threshold are pushed into a queue where controllers accept them, apply IATA delay codes with attributed minutes, and assign an owning department such as Ground Operations, Dispatch, or MCC. Follow-ups move through accepted, in-progress, and closed states with comment history, and the dashboard reports departure and arrival OTP against target alongside the most frequent delay causes.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-plane-departure"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="project-title">FlightOps Executive</h3>
                <p class="project-description">Network operations control centre with a live surveillance map, executive KPIs, disruption intelligence, and route administration.</p>
                <ul class="project-features">
                    <li>Live airborne tracking map</li>
                    <li>On-time performance and movement KPIs</li>
                    <li>Disruption and delay-reason analytics</li>
                    <li>Route, fleet, and user administration</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span class="tech-tag">ASP.NET Core</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">Razor Pages</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">SignalR</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">EF Core</span>
                </div>
                <a class="project-demo-link" href="/demos/flightops/">
                    <i class="fas fa-play"></i> View demo
                </a>
                <button class="project-expand-btn" onclick="toggleProjectDetails(this)">
                    <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i> Learn More
                </button>
                <div class="project-details">
                    <p>ASP.NET Core Razor Pages with EF Core and SignalR. A fixed route network seeds the daily schedule, and hosted background services advance every flight through boarding, departure, en-route, and arrival while injecting delays, cancellations, and disruption records. The operations map interpolates aircraft positions between origin and destination in real time, sitting alongside movement and OTP counters, status and delay-reason breakdowns, a critical-alert feed, and admin screens for route dispatch, instant flight injection, and role-based user access.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-exclamation-triangle"></i>
                </div>
