                <p class="project-description">Crisis information and family-matching system supporting incident workflows, public forms, case review, matching, and reporting.</p>
                <ul class="project-features">
                    <li>Incident workflow support</li>
                    <li>Case review and matching</li>
                    <li>Public-facing forms</li>
                    <li>Reporting and insights</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span class="tech-tag">.NET</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">PostgreSQL</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">React</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">TypeScript</span>
                </div>
                <a class="project-demo-link" href="/demos/cfms/">
                    <i class="fas fa-play"></i> View demo
                </a>
                <button class="project-expand-btn" onclick="toggleProjectDetails(this)">
                    <i class="fas fa-chevron-down"></i> Learn More
                </button>
                <div class="project-details">
                    <p>.NET API with a React and TypeScript frontend over PostgreSQL. It handles incident creation and escalation, public enquiry forms for relatives, structured case files, and a reviewer-driven queue that matches enquiries against recovered records. Access is deliberately narrow: dashboards show aggregate counts only, and detailed reporting or exports sit behind separate role-restricted permissions.</p>
                </div>
            </div>

            <div class="project-card">
                <div class="project-icon">
                    <i class="fas fa-clipboard-list"></i>
                </div>
                <h3 class="project-title">TravelFairSimReg</h3>
                <p class="project-description">Registration and session-management workflow for travel fair and simulator events, from attendee sign-up through to the operating team's roster.</p>
                <ul class="project-features">
                    <li>Validated attendee registration forms</li>
                    <li>Session slots with capacity limits</li>
                    <li>Confirmation and reference records</li>
                    <li>Administrative registration overview</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="project-tech">
                    <span class="tech-tag">.NET</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">React</span>
                    <span class="tech-tag">SQL Server</span>
                </div>
                <a class="project-demo-link" href="/demos/travelfairsimreg/pages/registration.html?v=offline-demo-3" target="_blank" rel="noopener">
